WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.560
Chris Hemsworth doesn't want to return to
"the place where no man has gone before."

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.460
In an in-depth interview with Variety, he
revealed the real reason he turned down the

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.880
chance to reprise his role as George Kirk
in Star Trek 4.

00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:16.600
Hemsworth's Star Trek character ...the father
of Chris Pine's James T. Kirk ...only appeared

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.870
in the opening sequence of J.J. Abrams' 2009
Star Trek reboot ...and his character seemingly

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.800
perished after the Romulans attacked the Federation
starship USS Kelvin.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.880
"Sweetheart, can you hear me?"

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:28.500
"I can hear you."

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.820
"I love you so much.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.060
I love…"

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.840
Ever since then, franchise fans have wondered
whether the fallen officer will ever pop up

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.360
again in a future installment.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.180
Unfortunately, it sounds like that isn't going
to happen anytime soon.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:51.140
Hemsworth told Variety that he turned down
the chance to star in Star Trek 4 because

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:54.780
he didn't find the script particularly intriguing
or satisfying.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.560
More importantly, it sounds like he didn't
think the storyline ultimately earned the

00:00:58.560 --> 00:00:59.640
character's return.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.700
As he put it,

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.940
"I didn't feel like we landed on a reason
to revisit that yet.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.580
I didn't want to be underwhelmed by what I
was going to bring to the table."

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.920
What's interesting about these comments is
how they contradict an announcement Paramount

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.330
Pictures made about Hemsworth's involvement
in Star Trek 4.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:20.340
In 2016, the studio claimed the actor would
be returning to Star Trek 4, as would Chris

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:20.840
Pine.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.680
That announcement read in part:

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.080
"In the next installment of the epic space
adventure, Chris Pine's Captain Kirk will

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.940
cross paths with a man he never had a chance
to meet [...] his father.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.130
Chris Hemsworth, who appeared in 2009's Star
Trek, will return to the space saga as George

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.100
Kirk to star alongside Pine."

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:43.420
Between then and now, Hemsworth backed out
of the film ...as did Pine, evidently.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:48.300
In August 2018, The Hollywood Reporter ran
a story that claimed both actors parted ways

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.660
with Paramount and Skydance Media after the
companies reportedly backtracked on promised

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:53.160
deals.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:57.620
Following the disappointing box office performance
of Star Trek Beyond, Paramount reportedly

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:01.840
modified Hemsworth and Pine's deals in such
a way that they both would've had to take

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.180
significant pay cuts.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:08.140
Perhaps money was the major issue for both
Chrises, but for Hemsworth, it evidently wasn't

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.240
the only factor that led him to walk away
from Star Trek 4.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:15.520
Though it would've been truly amazing to see
Hemsworth return to the franchise, we understand

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:16.840
why he ultimately declined.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.020
Based on his statements, it sounds like he'd
still be interested in reprising the role

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.740
for a future installment ...just as long as
the script was super-solid.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.550
But based on what Hemsworth told Variety,
it sounds like the way George Kirk would've

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:33.320
figured into the storyline of Star Trek 4
was shaky at best.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.700
What's more, Hemsworth has become a household
name thanks to playing Thor in the Marvel

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:38.940
Cinematic Universe.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:43.160
At this point, it sounds like he only wants
to sign on to projects that he truly feels

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.180
passionate about.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.340
Since he's one of the hottest names in Hollywood
right now, he must be getting dozens of offers

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:48.980
on the hour.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:53.680
At the end of the day, Star Trek 4 simply
didn't tickle the Aussie actor's fancy, and

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.180
that's okay.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.480
It's not like he'll be out of work without
it.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:00.360
Sadly, Star Trek 4 may ultimately never get
off the ground.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:06.160
In April 2018, Paramount greenlit production
on two Star Trek features: one from Quentin

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.200
Tarantino, and one from British television
director S.J.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:09.700
Clarkson.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:15.440
But less than a year later, it was reported
that Star Trek 4 was, quote, "cancelled indefinitely."

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.660
Even though the studio pulled the plug on
the project, plenty of fans are still holding

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:23.280
out hope that Paramount will eventually bring
Star Trek 4 back to life.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.740
But even if they do decide to resurrect the
film, don't expect to see Hemsworth's pretty

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.530
face anywhere in the film.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.140
"Sweetheart, listen to me.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.140
I'm not gonna be there."

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:34.360
"No."

